From: Linux Build System <linux-build@example.com>
Date: Sat, 13 Jun 2026 11:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] efi/libstub: Add -std=gnu11 to CFLAGS for GCC 15+

GCC 15+ defaults to -std=gnu23, which makes 'bool', 'true' and 'false'
reserved keywords. The EFI libstub Makefile defines its own cflags
without including -std=gnu11, which causes build failures when the C
standard defaults to C23.

The boot/compressed Makefile already has -std=gnu89 from the realmode
patch.  The EFI libstub is a separate compilation unit that needs its
own -std=gnu11 fix.

Signed-off-by: Linux Build System <linux-build@example.com>

diff --git a/drivers/firmware/efi/libstub/Makefile b/drivers/firmware/efi/libstub/Makefile
index f7a20bf..6cb15d3 100644
--- a/drivers/firmware/efi/libstub/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/firmware/efi/libstub/Makefile
@@ -10,7 +10,7 @@
 cflags-$(CONFIG_X86_32)		:= -march=i386
 cflags-$(CONFIG_X86_64)		:= -mcmodel=small
 cflags-$(CONFIG_X86)		+= -m$(BITS) -D__KERNEL__ -O2 \
-				   -fPIC -fno-strict-aliasing -mno-red-zone \
+				   -std=gnu11 -fPIC -fno-strict-aliasing -mno-red-zone \
 				   -mno-mmx -mno-sse -fshort-wchar \
 				   -Wno-pointer-sign \
 				   $(call cc-disable-warning, address-of-packed-member) \
